---
title: Warm Potato Salad
description: Earl's-inspired warm salad of roasted baby potatoes and corn tossed with crispy bacon and a creamy Parmesan dressing.
course: salad
cook time: 45 minutes
source: https://www.leppfarmmarket.com/earls-warm-potato-salad/
image: https://www.leppfarmmarket.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/IMG_1249.jpg
tags:
  - potato
  - bacon
  - warm salad
  - roasted
---

In a small bowl, combine @mayonnaise{2/3%cup}, @sour cream{1/3%cup}, @parmesan cheese{1/4%cup}(finely grated), @lemon juice{1%tbsp}, @chives{1%tbsp}(finely chopped) and season lightly with @salt and @pepper to make the dressing. Season lightly since the bacon and potatoes add saltiness; you can adjust later.

Preheat the #oven{} to 425°F.

In a #skillet{}, fry @bacon{4%slices} over medium heat until crispy, then drain, cool, and chop into ½-inch pieces.

Halve @baby potatoes{2%lbs}, toss with @garlic{1-2%cloves}(minced) and @olive oil{3%tbsp}, spread on a #parchment-lined sheet pan{}, and bake for ~{20%minutes}.

Toss @corn kernels{1%cup}(drained if frozen) with the remaining @olive oil{1%tbsp}, add to the potatoes, and bake another ~{25%minutes}.

Transfer the potatoes and corn to a #large bowl{}, toss with the dressing and bacon, adjust seasoning, garnish with @chives for garnish, and serve.
